// The public per-claim Sahyog Vivran — Story 11b.3 (Task 4; AC1, AC3, AC5, AC8).
//
// ⭐⛔ READ THIS FIRST — THE TIER-LEAK LEG ON THIS SURFACE IS **OPERATIVE FROM ITS FIRST COMMIT**.
// `sahyogVivranSurfaceFieldIds(model)` returns a NON-EMPTY set, so `evaluateSnapshot` actually
// evaluates the leak rules here and a planted `authenticated_member`-tier or UNDECLARED field at
// `public` FAILS a run that previously passed. ⛔ A green scan over an armed-but-empty leg proves
// nothing.
//
// ⭐ WHAT THIS PAGE RENDERS: ONE drive's own record — which pool it was, how it closed, how many
// contributions were CONFIRMED as money received, and, when the claim reached it by appeal, the
// non-PII reversal lineage.
// ⛔ EVERY value goes through `<MatrixField>`, so `getVisibility()` is the ONLY thing deciding what
// appears.
//
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ⭐⭐ IT NAMES ⛔ NOBODY — ⛔ NOT THE DECEASED MEMBER, ⛔ NOT A CONTRIBUTOR, ⛔ NOT A VERIFIER,
// ⛔ NOT A NOMINEE. THAT IS THE CORRECT STATE, ⛔ NOT A BROKEN ONE.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// It is what the D6(b) split bought (`2026-09-02-182` cl.2): with ⛔ no `pii_tier: 1` field at
// `tier: public`, this surface needs ⛔ no `tier1_public_exception`, ⛔ no `RULED_TIER1_PUBLIC_
// EXCEPTIONS` entry and ⛔ no Panel ruling — so ⛔ nothing outside this repository can block it.
// ⇒ **11b.3b** adds the named-identity render layer (`2026-09-02-173` / `-174`) and **11b.3a** the
// nominee bank presentation (`2026-08-28-160` cl.10, `-165` cl.1/cl.3), each WITH its allowlist entry
// in the same commit. ⛔ Do not "fill the gap" here.
//
// ⛔⛔ AND FOUR PRODUCERS THE EPIC AC NAMES DO ⛔ NOT EXIST — verifier profile pages (⛔ zero hits in
// the repo), the family story (11b.4, `backlog`), the memorial components (11b.5, `backlog`) and
// `<StatCardStrip>` (C-3, ⛔ no producer AND ⛔ no owner). ⭐ The ruled posture is 11a.5's third path
// and C-4 SURVIVED `-160` untouched: *render nothing when empty* — ⛔ never a fabricated row, ⛔ never
// a "coming soon" placeholder. ⚠ *A silent section is the CORRECT state, ⛔ not a bug to close
// quickly.* ⛔ Do ⛔ not stub `<StatCardStrip>`: a stub asserts an aggregate nothing computes, and
// building any of the four re-commits SD-1.
//
// ⛔⛔ AND ⛔ NO RUPEE FIGURE. `amountRaisedInr = confirmedCount × fixedAmount` is SHIPPED and ruled
// canonical (Story 9.12 D3) and **D1(b)** ruled it CONSUMED — but it lives behind the `@twt/ui` fence
// this story does ⛔ not lift, so the amount MOVES to **11b.3b**. ⛔ Re-deriving the multiplication
// here is **D1(c)**, REFUSED. ⚠ The interim asymmetry (a count here, an amount in the member app) is
// ORDERING, ⛔ not a ruling, and ⛔ NOT a second D7 inversion.
//
// ⛔⛔ AND ⛔ NO SESSION, EVER: ⛔ no `Astro.cookies`, ⛔ no auth read of `Astro.request.headers`,
// ⛔ no `Astro.session`, ⛔ no `isAuthenticated` prop on `<AuthenticatedFragment>`. ⭐ Every visitor
// sees BYTE-IDENTICAL markup ([[project_no_browser_member_token_surface]]). ⚠ SD-2 is RE-PURPOSED
// onto the POST-campaign masking state (`2026-08-28-164` A2) — ⛔ not dissolved; the post-masking
// authenticated presentation is a SEPARATE FUTURE DECISION, ⛔ not carried and ⛔ not foreclosed.
//
// ⛔⛔ BUILT IS ⛔ NOT PUBLISHED. DPDPA clearance for this surface was LIFTED (`2026-08-28-160` cl.7)
// on clause 4's model. ⚠ ⛔ Never write that counsel is not engaged — **Adv. Mohit Agrawal** has been
// engaged since 2026-06-21 (`2026-08-24-158`); the correct form is *"counsel has not reviewed X"*.
// ⭐ What keeps this surface dark is DEPLOYMENT plus the counsel/Panel process — ⛔ never a code
// mechanism, and ⛔ never the publication kill switch, which is an EMERGENCY control that defaults to
// ENABLED by design ([[project_directory_launch_gated_on_killswitch_ui]]).
//
// ── ⛔ WHY THE DATA COMES OVER HTTP AND NOT FROM A LOCAL READ ────────────────────────────────
// ⚠ ⛔ NOT for the reason the two sibling surfaces give. Theirs is the Tier-1 KYC decrypt; this read
// selects ⛔ no Tier-1 column and costs ZERO KMS round-trips, which is the point of the split.
// ⭐ THE OTHER TWO REASONS STILL HOLD, and here the first is load-bearing: an anti-enumeration ceiling
// (a rate-limit store) and an audit line (the BYPASSRLS service pool), ⛔ neither of which
// `apps/public` has. The identifier is SEQUENTIAL and controls 2/3 are structurally N/A (D11(a)), so
// `limits.search` is the ONLY bound on walking it. ⛔ Do not add a `withPublicScope` read here.
//
// House shape, mirroring `sahyog.astro` and `members.astro`: thin frontmatter, ALL display logic in
// the pure `lib/sahyog-vivran-render.ts`, explicit `namespace` on every `t()` call (⚠ `t()` defaults
// to `common` and THROWS on a miss — the `{{max}}` vs `{max}` defect that made `/members` throw on
// EVERY request at 11a.2 was exactly this shape, and no test caught it because every test bypassed
// `t()`).
import { getLocale, isLocale, t } from '@twt/i18n';
import type { Locale } from '@twt/i18n';
import { passport } from '@twt/domain';

import MatrixField from '../../components/MatrixField.astro';
import PublicShell from '../../layouts/PublicShell.astro';
import { getDb } from '../../lib/db.server.js';
import { visibilityOf } from '../../lib/matrix.server.js';
import {
  buildSahyogVivranOutageView,
  buildSahyogVivranView,
  type SahyogVivranLabels,
} from '../../lib/sahyog-vivran-render.js';
import { buildForwardedFor, fetchSahyogVivran } from '../../lib/sahyog-vivran.server.js';
import { ACTIVE_PARIWAR_ID } from '../../lib/pariwar.server.js';

// ⭐⭐ STORY 11b.10 — THE ROUTE PARAMETER IS THE DRIVE'S **OPAQUE PUBLIC ADDRESS TOKEN**, and the
// FILE NAME is that parameter: `[driveToken].astro`, ⛔ no longer `[poolCanonicalIdentifier].astro`.
// `2026-09-03-184` **(B)**, Trustee-ratified — the sequential `P-YYYY-MM-###` made this whole
// surface walkable by COUNTING, and since 11b.3a that walk reached four decrypted Tier-1 bank fields.
// ⛔⛔ EXACTLY ONE ADDRESS FORM: ⛔ do not add a second route, a redirect, or an alias accepting the
// bare identifier "for old links" — that is a lock beside an open door (Trap 3). ⭐ The identifier is
// RETAINED and is still RENDERED below via `<MatrixField field="pool_canonical_identifier">`.
const { driveToken: rawDriveToken } = Astro.params;

// ── Locale + branding (cache-safe: no session, no member state) ──────────────
const langParam = Astro.url.searchParams.get('lang');
// ⚠ `accept-language` is a CONTENT-NEGOTIATION header, ⛔ not an auth signal. Reading it is the
// house pattern on every public page and does ⛔ not breach the "no auth-derived branching" rule —
// the page sets `Vary: Accept-Language` so the edge keys on it honestly.
const acceptLanguage = Astro.request.headers.get('accept-language') ?? undefined;
const db = getDb().db;
const passportRow = await passport.getPariwarPassportCached(db, ACTIVE_PARIWAR_ID);
const locale: Locale = isLocale(langParam)
  ? langParam
  : getLocale({ pariwarPassportLocale: passportRow?.localeDefault, acceptLanguage });
const trustName =
  (locale === 'hi'
    ? (passportRow?.displayNameHi ?? passportRow?.displayNameEn)
    : (passportRow?.displayNameEn ?? passportRow?.displayNameHi)) ?? 'Sahyog Vivran';
const branding = passportRow?.brandingBundle ?? null;

// ⛔ NOTE THE ABSENCE: there is no `withPublicScope` pool, claim or member read here, and there must
// not be one. The passport read above is branding, ⛔ not drive data.

// ⚠ EXPLICIT NAMESPACE ON EVERY CALL — `t()` defaults to `common` and THROWS on a miss.
const tr = (key: string, params?: Record<string, string | number>) =>
  t(key, params, { locale, namespace: 'sahyog-vivran' });

const labels: SahyogVivranLabels = {
  pageTitle: tr('page.title'),
  pageIntro: tr('page.intro'),
  factsGroupLabel: tr('facts.group_label'),
  labelDriveCode: tr('label.drive_code'),
  labelPoolLetter: tr('label.pool_letter'),
  labelDistrict: tr('label.district'),
  labelClosedOn: tr('label.closed_on'),
  labelContributions: tr('label.contributions'),
  labelStatus: tr('label.status'),
  districtUnknown: tr('value.district_unknown'),
  statusCollecting: tr('status.collecting'),
  statusActive: tr('status.active'),
  statusArchive: tr('status.archive'),
  collectingTitle: tr('collecting.title'),
  collectingBody: tr('collecting.body'),
  // ⭐ THREE DISTINCT STRINGS, one per opaque outcome token — ⛔ and NONE of them compares to a
  // target, quotes a percentage, or names a shortfall. `classifyCycleOutcome` already quarantined the
  // numbers upstream; this is the second place that quarantine has to hold, because COPY is where a
  // shortfall would actually surface. ⚠ `microcopy.yaml`'s `pool-reality-comparison` tone rule bites
  // `fell short` / `shortfall` / `\d+% of the target` / `लक्ष्य से कम` at PR time.
  outcomeFullyFunded: tr('outcome.fully_funded'),
  outcomeUnderFunded: tr('outcome.under_funded'),
  outcomePartial: tr('outcome.partial'),
  appealTitle: tr('appeal.title'),
  appealLineage: tr('appeal.lineage'),
  labelAppealStage: tr('label.appeal_stage'),
  // ⚠ Interpolated THROUGH `t()`, ⛔ never by local string surgery — the 11a.2 `{{max}}` vs `{max}`
  // defect threw on EVERY request and no test caught it, because every test bypassed `t()`.
  appealStage: (stage: number) => tr('appeal.stage', { stage }),
  appealReversedOn: tr('appeal.reversed_on'),
  dispositionNewEvidence: tr('disposition.new_evidence_presented'),
  dispositionProceduralCorrection: tr('disposition.procedural_correction'),
  dispositionReconsideration: tr('disposition.reconsideration_on_merits'),
  contributionsCount: (count: number) => tr('value.contributions_count', { count }),
  outageTitle: tr('outage.title'),
  outageBody: tr('outage.body'),
  // ── ⭐ Story 11b.3a — the nominee block, ⭐⛔ REDUCED BY STORY 11b.11 ─────────────────────────
  // ⚠ `t()` THROWS on a missing key, so every retirement below moved in BOTH locales in this same
  // commit. ✅ Grepped first: the `sahyog-vivran` namespace has ⛔ no other consumer.
  bankTitle: tr('bank.title'),
  bankGroupLabel: tr('bank.group_label'),
  // ⭐ THE EQUALITY STATEMENT IS COPY, ⛔ not a comment: a reader with two names in front of them
  // will otherwise infer a preference from the order. `account_rank` is row identity (Story 9.9).
  // ⚠⛔ RE-KEYED from `bank.equal_destinations` — after `2026-09-04-190` cl.1 there is ⛔ no
  // destination on this page to choose between, and the old sentence *"Either account can be
  // used"* asserted an affordance the page no longer offers.
  bankEqualNominees: tr('bank.equal_nominees'),
  // ⛔⛔ ⛔ NO ORDINAL. It was `(rank) => tr('bank.account_label', { rank })` ⇒ *"Account 1"* /
  // *"Account 2"* announced to screen readers only, contradicting the equality this very page
  // states in copy. ⛔ Do ⛔ not re-introduce the interpolation.
  bankAccountLabel: tr('bank.account_label'),
  // ⭐⛔ THE RULED PUBLIC WORDING — `2026-09-04-190` cl.2, Trustee-ratified: **"Nominee Name"**,
  // ⛔ never *"Account holder"*. ⚠ The KEY still says `account_holder` on purpose: the key names the
  // DATA (6.8's D1 — ⛔ no FK to `member_nominees`, ⛔ no rank, ⛔ no match rule), the value is the
  // ruled PRESENTATION, and the ruling itself draws exactly that line.
  labelAccountHolder: tr('label.account_holder'),
};

// ── Cache headers (AC2's `edge_cacheable` declaration) ──────────────────────
// ⛔ SET BEFORE THE 404 BRANCH, DELIBERATELY — the `blog/[postId].astro` precedent, and for the same
// mechanical reason: `checkCachePolicyReconciliation` scans this file's WHOLE SOURCE for the call's
// presence, ⛔ not per-branch, so a header set only after an early `return` reads as compliant to the
// gate while the 404 response ships with none. An unknown identifier 404s deterministically for that
// URL forever, so caching that is correct, ⛔ not merely convenient.
//
// ⚠⛔ AND THE ACCEPTED COST IS THE SAME ONE `/sahyog` CARRIES: at `s-maxage=300` a pulled Pariwar
// keeps being served from every warm PoP for up to five minutes, and the origin-side rate limit sees
// only cache MISSES (a cached hit never reaches the origin). ⛔ Direct SQL is NOT the operational
// fallback, and ⛔ do not "fix" the edge-blindness by making this surface `private_no_store` — that
// discards the edge for a public surface and was already REJECTED at 11a.3.
Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'public, max-age=60, s-maxage=300');
Astro.response.headers.set('Vary', 'Accept-Language');

// ⭐⛔ A MISSING OR BLANK ADDRESS IS A 404, ⛔ NOT AN ERROR AND ⛔ NOT A REDIRECT — the same answer an
// unknown drive gets, because a distinguishable *"malformed"* answer is an enumeration signal.
// ⚠⭐ THE GROUND MOVED AT 11b.10 AND IS RESTATED: it used to be *"…on a SEQUENTIAL identifier"*. The
// address is no longer sequential — what makes the sameness matter now is that a distinguishable
// refusal would let an attacker TEST guessed tokens, which is the oracle the token exists to close.
const driveToken = (rawDriveToken ?? '').trim();

const fetched =
  driveToken === ''
    ? ({ ok: false, reason: 'not_found' } as const)
    : await fetchSahyogVivran({
        driveToken,
        // ⛔ `Astro.clientAddress` ONLY, via the REUSED `buildForwardedFor`. The inbound
        // `X-Forwarded-For` header is deliberately NOT read — it is caller-supplied, and `apps/api`'s
        // `trustProxy: true` keys on the LEFTMOST chain entry, so forwarding it hands the attacker
        // the rate-limit key (`2026-08-21-145` cl.2). ⛔ Do not "restore the full chain".
        forwardedFor: buildForwardedFor(Astro.clientAddress),
      });

// ⭐⛔ 404 IS THE ANSWER FOR EVERY *"nothing to show"* CASE, AND THEY ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL.
// *"No such drive"*, *"exists but is not visible at this surface's predicate"*, *"this Pariwar's
// public surfaces are switched off"* and *"the identifier was malformed"* all land here. ⛔ Never an
// error distinguishing them — a distinguishable miss is an ENUMERATION SIGNAL, and the identifier is
// sequential. ⛔ A plain 404, ⛔ never a redirect: a `Location` header has no effect on a non-3xx
// response, and a prior surface's version of that was dead weight masquerading as a redirect.
if (!fetched.ok && (fetched.reason === 'not_found' || fetched.reason === 'rejected')) {
  return new Response(null, { status: 404, headers: Astro.response.headers });
}

// ⭐⛔ AN OUTAGE IS ⛔ NOT A 404, AND THE TWO MUST NEVER COLLAPSE. *"We could not load this just now"*
// is a statement about THIS REQUEST'S luck; *"there is no such drive"* is a statement about the public
// record. ⚠ Rendering the second on the first's evidence is the most misleading thing this surface
// could say about a family's drive. 503 + `Retry-After` + `no-store` is the honest shape — ⛔ not 500
// (the failure is upstream and transient, and this page rendered correctly), and ⛔ not 200 (a page
// that says "could not be loaded" at 200 is a lie to every cache, crawler and uptime check).
const apiUnavailable = !fetched.ok;
const view = fetched.ok
  ? buildSahyogVivranView(fetched.data, labels)
  // ⛔ NO ARGUMENT (11b.10): the URL carries an opaque ADDRESS, ⛔ not a drive code, so there is
  // nothing to echo — and echoing the address would render it into a classified field.
  : buildSahyogVivranOutageView();

if (apiUnavailable) {
  Astro.response.status = 503;
  Astro.response.headers.set('Retry-After', '60');
  // ⛔ OVERRIDES the shared-cache header above: an outage is a statement about this request, and
  // pinning it into a shared edge for five minutes would outlive the failure it describes.
  Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store');
}

const model = view.model;

// ⭐ RESOLVED ONCE PER RENDER. The matrix cannot vary within a page, and asking `getVisibility()`
// repeatedly would be an N+1 on a constant. ⛔ `visibilityOf` is the ONLY thing consulted — ⛔ no
// local tier comparison, ⛔ no second viewer ceiling.
//
// ⭐⛔ `drive_status` NEEDS THIS GUARD FOR THE SAME REASON `/sahyog`'s DOES, AND IT IS SHARPER HERE.
// The status is disclosed STRUCTURALLY as well as in its own cell: the "still collecting" block below
// renders ⟺ the drive is `collecting`, and the close-of-cycle framing renders ⟺ it is not. ⇒ flipping
// `drive_status.tier` to `authenticated_member` in the YAML would suppress the CELL and change
// ⛔ nothing about what the page discloses, while the leak gate stayed GREEN because the field id is
// still declared. ⛔ This guard does not hide those blocks — hiding them is a real design change (the
// live/closed distinction IS this page's structure). ⭐ What it does is make the inertness IMPOSSIBLE
// TO INTRODUCE QUIETLY: a matrix verdict this page cannot honour now FAILS THE RENDER.
const driveStatusVisible = visibilityOf('sahyog-vivran', 'drive_status', 'public').visible;
if (!driveStatusVisible) {
  throw new Error(
    '[sahyog-vivran] the matrix suppresses `drive_status` for `sahyog-vivran` at the `public` tier, ' +
      'but this page discloses it STRUCTURALLY — through the still-collecting block and the ' +
      'close-of-cycle framing block, which render on opposite sides of that very value — and has no ' +
      'single cell to suppress. Honouring that verdict requires redesigning the page, not a config ' +
      'change. Restore the tier, or make the change deliberately.',
  );
}
---

<PublicShell
  locale={locale}
  title={labels.pageTitle}
  description={labels.pageIntro}
  trustName={trustName}
  branding={branding}
  noindex={true}
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-8">
    <p class="mb-4"><a href="/sahyog" class="text-sm text-blue-600 hover:underline">← {tr('page.title')}</a></p>

    <header class="mb-6">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold">{labels.pageTitle}</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">{labels.pageIntro}</p>
    </header>

    {apiUnavailable ? (
      <section class="rounded border border-gray-300 p-4">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">{labels.outageTitle}</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">{labels.outageBody}</p>
      </section>
    ) : (
      <>
        {/*
          ⭐ AC8 — FAMILY 13 (Semantic accessibility, AI-11a-3) IN ITS **WEB** FORM.
          ⚠⛔ Family 13 is written in REACT-NATIVE vocabulary and its worked example is
          `apps/mobile/components/panchayat/PinnedItem.tsx`; `accessible` / `accessibilityLabel` /
          `accessibilityValue` are RN props with ⛔ NO HTML equivalent. ⛔ Do ⛔ not record family 13 as
          held by pointing at that file. The web translation this story owes, written down:
            (a) the labelled container is a REAL GROUPING ELEMENT carrying a `role` AND an
                `aria-label` — ⛔ never a bare `<div>` carrying a label no role announces. Here that is
                the `role="group"` + `aria-label` below, and the `<dl>` whose own semantics pair each
                term with its value.
            (b) a role implying a VALUE carries `aria-valuenow` / `aria-valuetext`. ⭐ This page has
                ⛔ NO such role — there is no meter, no progressbar and no slider, deliberately: the
                progress meter is `@twt/ui`'s and D1(b) did ⛔ not authorise it here. ⇒ (b) is held
                VACUOUSLY, and that is stated rather than left to be inferred.
            (c) a role implying INTERACTION is a real `<a>` / `<button>` — the one interactive element
                on this page is the back link above, a real `<a href>` that works with JS disabled.
            (d) ⛔ NO announced-order dependence on visual order: every value is announced through its
                own `<dt>` label, so the reading order carries its own meaning and a CSS reflow cannot
                change what is said.
          ⛔ NO a11y CI gate is minted here — AI-11a-3 routes that to *"checklist/invariant family 13
          first; a CI gate ⛔ only if later mechanically justified"* (C-2: 19 gates in `scripts/`, ⛔ none
          a11y, while Story 11b.8 makes an accessibility audit a LAUNCH-BLOCKER).
        */}
        <section role="group" aria-label={labels.factsGroupLabel} class="rounded border border-gray-300 p-4">
          <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.labelPoolLetter}</dt>
              <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="pool_letter_code" viewerContext="public" value={model.poolLetterCode} /></dd>
            </div>
            {/* ⭐⛔ THE `<dt>`/`<dd>` PAIR IS SUPPRESSED TOGETHER (review 2026-09-04) — the same
                rule `visibleSahyogColumns()` enforces for the index's `<th>`/`<td>`.
                ⚠ THE CASE THAT MADE THIS REAL: `buildSahyogVivranOutageView()` sets
                `poolCanonicalIdentifier: ''` (the 503 page deliberately does ⛔ not echo the address
                back), `outputForVerdict` maps `''` → `null`, and `<MatrixField>` then correctly
                emits NOTHING — leaving a "Drive code" TERM with ⛔ no DEFINITION. A screen reader
                announces the label and then falls silent, which is worse than not announcing it.
                ⛔ Not echoing the address on the outage page is RIGHT; the orphaned `<dt>` was the
                unhandled consequence of it. */}
            {model.poolCanonicalIdentifier !== '' && (
              <div>
                <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.labelDriveCode}</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="pool_canonical_identifier" viewerContext="public" value={model.poolCanonicalIdentifier} /></dd>
              </div>
            )}
            <div>
              <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.labelStatus}</dt>
              <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="drive_status" viewerContext="public" value={model.driveStatus} /></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.labelDistrict}</dt>
              {/*
                ⚠ `?? districtUnknown` — a missing posting row renders the "Not recorded" copy, ⛔ not
                a blank cell. That is a DIFFERENT nothing from a matrix suppression, which
                `<MatrixField>` renders as literally nothing.
              */}
              <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="district" viewerContext="public" value={model.district ?? labels.districtUnknown} /></dd>
            </div>
            {/*
              ⭐⛔ THE CLOSE DATE'S CELL IS OMITTED ENTIRELY WHILE THE DRIVE IS COLLECTING, ⛔ not
              rendered with a "not yet" placeholder. There is no close instant to state, and inventing
              a marker for it would be the announced omission this family of surfaces forbids.
            */}
            {model.driveClosedAt !== null && (
              <div>
                <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.labelClosedOn}</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="drive_closed_at" viewerContext="public" value={model.driveClosedAt} /></dd>
              </div>
            )}
            <div>
              <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.labelContributions}</dt>
              {/*
                ⛔ A COUNT, ⛔ never a sum and ⛔ never a score — and there is deliberately ⛔ NO rupee
                figure anywhere on this page (D1(b) moved it to 11b.3b; D1(c) is REFUSED).
              */}
              <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="confirmed_contribution_count" viewerContext="public" value={model.confirmedContributionCount} /></dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        {/*
          ⭐ AC3's HONEST LIVE-DRIVE COPY — ⛔ never an estimate, ⛔ never a projected final amount,
          ⛔ never an "X% confirmed so far" frame that exposes the attested↔confirmed gap.
        */}
        {model.isCollecting && (
          <section class="mt-6 rounded border border-gray-300 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">{labels.collectingTitle}</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">{labels.collectingBody}</p>
          </section>
        )}

        {/*
          ⭐ Pool-Reality #2 framing. ⚠ RENDERS NOTHING when null — the drive is still collecting, or
          ⛔ no expectation was ever set (zero assignees). ⛔ Never a fabricated outcome: `0 >= 0` is
          vacuously true and once published "the cycle closed with the support it needed" beside
          "0 confirmed" (the 11b.1 review finding), which is why the null arm exists.
        */}
        {model.closeOfCycleFraming !== null && (
          <section class="mt-6 rounded border border-gray-300 p-4">
            <p class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="close_of_cycle_framing" viewerContext="public" value={model.closeOfCycleFraming} /></p>
          </section>
        )}

        {/*
          ⭐ AC5 — THE "REVERSED BY APPEAL" LINEAGE, DERIVED AT REQUEST TIME (D12(a): ⛔ no queue,
          ⛔ no consumer, ⛔ no publication record).
          ⛔⛔ IT NEVER CARRIES RATIONALE TEXT OR A REVIEWER IDENTITY — those live on the
          `claim.appeal_stageN_reviewed` DECISION event's Tier-1 metadata row and are ⛔ NEVER public.
          `claim.reversed` is the PUBLISH SIGNAL, ⛔ not the decision.
          ⚠ RENDERS NOTHING when the claim was never reversed — ⛔ no "not reversed" marker, which
          would publish a fact about claims that were NOT appealed.
        */}
        {model.wasReversedByAppeal && (
          <section class="mt-6 rounded border border-gray-300 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">{labels.appealTitle}</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">{labels.appealLineage}</p>
            <dl class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <div>
                <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.labelAppealStage}</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="appeal_reversal_stage" viewerContext="public" value={model.appealReversalStage} /></dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.appealReversedOn}</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="appeal_reversal_at" viewerContext="public" value={model.appealReversalAt} /></dd>
              </div>
              <div class="sm:col-span-2">
                <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="appeal_disposition_category" viewerContext="public" value={model.appealDispositionCategory} /></dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </section>
        )}

        {/*
          ⭐⭐ STORY 11b.3a — THE NOMINEE BLOCK, ⭐⛔ **WITHDRAWN DOWN TO ONE NAME BY STORY 11b.11.**

          ⛔⛔ WHAT STOOD HERE, kept as the record: bank name, branch, account holder, account number
          (full, or the localised "Account ending in NNNN" once masked), IFSC and UPI ID, under the
          heading "Where the money goes" and the group label "Bank details for this drive", with a
          masked-projection note. `2026-08-28-160` cl.10(a) authorised it: the Panel did ⛔ not treat
          public bank details as an automatic reason to prohibit publication, and the transparency
          benefit during an active Sahyog Drive was ACCEPTED.

          ⭐⭐ `2026-09-04-190` cl.1 (Trustee-ratified — Dhiraj Rahul, Kalpana Bharti) REMOVES the
          banking coordinates from this surface, and `2026-09-04-191` cl.1 removes the UPI ID with
          them. ⭐ cl.2 KEEPS the name, under the ruled public wording **"Nominee Name"**.
          ⇒ ⛔ this block renders ⛔ NO account number, ⛔ no last-4, ⛔ no IFSC, ⛔ no UPI ID, ⛔ no
          bank and ⛔ no branch. They are ABSENT FROM THE WIRE, ⛔ not hidden here — the withdrawal is
          structural at the contract, the domain read and the API boundary.

          ⛔⛔ THE FRAME MOVED WITH THE ROWS. A section headed *"Where the money goes"* naming a
          destination the page no longer shows, or grouped as *"Bank details for this drive"* while
          containing ⛔ no bank details, is the same defect as a row that should have gone and did
          not — prose outliving the thing it describes. ⭐ Both are re-worded, in BOTH locales.

          ⛔⛔ RENDERS NOTHING WHEN THERE ARE NO ACCOUNTS — ⛔ no "not recorded" marker, ⛔ no
          placeholder. The claim's bank details may simply never have been collected (6.8's AC3
          absence signal), and an omission that announces itself is an enumeration signal.

          ⛔⛔ THE RECORDED NAMES ARE **EQUAL**, and the page SAYS SO — ⚠ but ⛔ ONLY WHEN THERE IS
          MORE THAN ONE. `accountRank` is composite-PK row identity — ⛔ not a priority, ⛔ not a
          nominee rank, ⛔ not a split, ⛔ not routing (Story 9.9's re-scope). A one-element array is
          EXPLICITLY LEGAL, and the old standing sentence *"Either account can be used. Neither one
          is preferred over the other."* sat beside ONE card on such a claim and invited the reader
          to infer a second was being WITHHELD — on the page whose whole purpose is that nothing is
          hidden. ⇒ gated on `length > 1`, and re-worded to speak about the RECORD, ⛔ not about
          paying.

          ⛔⛔ AND THE PER-ACCOUNT `aria-label` NO LONGER ANNOUNCES AN ORDINAL. It rendered "Account
          1" / "Account 2" while the sighted page deliberately showed two identical UNNUMBERED
          boxes — `surface-fields.ts` maps `accountRank: null` precisely because an ordinal "would
          put an ordering that implies preference onto the page". ⇒ the equality the page states in
          copy was contradicted by its own output, in the direction ⛔ only assistive-tech users
          experience, and the field-classification gate was STRUCTURALLY BLIND to it because the
          value reached the DOM via `aria-label` rather than `<MatrixField>`. ⭐ The group is now
          named by what it IS. ⛔ Do ⛔ not re-introduce a rank.

          ⚠⛔ THE NAME IS ⛔ NOT LINKED TO A DECLARED NOMINEE IN THE DATA. 6.8's D1 removed that
          linkage DELIBERATELY — ⛔ no FK to `member_nominees`, ⛔ no rank, ⛔ no match rule — and that
          reasoning is about the SCHEMA and ⛔ STANDS. ⭐ `-190` cl.2 is Trustee-ratified and rules
          the PUBLIC WORDING; ⛔ do ⛔ not "reconcile" the two by adding a join or a match rule.
          ⚠⛔ AND THE RESIDUAL IS STATED, because this page now asserts it to the internet: the
          account holder MAY NOT BE THE NOMINEE, and ⛔ no verifier, ⛔ no state trustee and ⛔ no
          correcting admin can READ this value to notice (the only read-back is a PRESENCE view).
          ⇒ the one field that survives the withdrawal is UNVERIFIED and, today, UNVERIFIABLE.
          ROUTED at `deferred-work.md` (`D5-subject`), ⛔ not built here, ⛔ not hidden.

          ⛔ NO MASKING HAPPENS ON THIS PAGE, and now there is nothing left for it to happen TO.
          ⛔⛔ MASKING WAS ⛔ NOT DELETED — `-190` cl.4 RETAINS `isNomineeBankMasked`, the schedule
          table, its permission key, its admin surface and every test. ⚠ It has ⛔ NO PUBLIC CONSUMER;
          ⛔ do ⛔ not describe it as a live safeguard anywhere until it has one.

          ⭐ AC7 — FAMILY 13 IN ITS **WEB** FORM, same translation as the facts block above: each
          account is a REAL GROUPING ELEMENT with a `role` AND an `aria-label`, and its `<dl>` pairs
          the term with its value, so the announced order carries its own meaning.
        */}
        {model.nomineeAccounts.length > 0 && (
          <section role="group" aria-label={labels.bankGroupLabel} class="mt-6 rounded border border-gray-300 p-4">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">{labels.bankTitle}</h2>
            {/* ⭐ RENDERED ⛔ ONLY WHEN THERE IS MORE THAN ONE NAME — see the block comment.
                ⛔ Gated on accounts that actually RENDER a name, ⛔ not on the raw array length: a
                failed decrypt on one account (`nomineeAccountHolderName: null`) means only one name
                is visible, and "recorded equally" must not be claimed beside it. */}
            {model.nomineeAccounts.filter((a) => a.nomineeAccountHolderName !== null).length > 1 && (
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">{labels.bankEqualNominees}</p>
            )}
            {model.nomineeAccounts.map((account) => (
              <section
                role="group"
                aria-label={
                  account.nomineeAccountHolderName !== null
                    ? `${labels.labelAccountHolder}: ${account.nomineeAccountHolderName}`
                    : labels.bankAccountLabel
                }
                class="mt-4 rounded border border-gray-200 p-3"
              >
                <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
                  {/* ⭐⛔ THE ⛔ ONLY ROW LEFT. `null` on a failed decrypt ⇒ the cell is omitted
                      ENTIRELY — ⛔ never a placeholder, ⛔ never a "not provided" marker.
                      ⚠ The `<dt>` reads "Nominee Name" (`2026-09-04-190` cl.2); the matrix field id
                      stays `nominee_account_holder_name`, which is what the DATA is.
                      ⭐ [Review, corrected] The group's `aria-label` INTERPOLATES the recorded name
                      itself when present, ⛔ not a shared static string and ⛔ not an
                      `aria-labelledby` pointing at this `<dt>` — the `<dt>` is the field LABEL
                      ("Nominee Name"), identical for every account, so referencing it as the
                      accessible name (the first version of this fix) computed the SAME name for
                      both groups and fixed nothing. Interpolating the actual value is what makes
                      the two EQUAL accounts distinguishable by content, never by ordinal — and when
                      the recorded name happens to be identical, or a decrypt fails, the fallback is
                      honest: sighted and assistive-tech users get the SAME distinguishing power,
                      never less. */}
                  {account.nomineeAccountHolderName !== null && (
                    <div>
                      <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">{labels.labelAccountHolder}</dt>
                      <dd class="text-sm"><MatrixField surface="sahyog-vivran" field="nominee_account_holder_name" viewerContext="public" value={account.nomineeAccountHolderName} /></dd>
                    </div>
                  )}
                </dl>
              </section>
            ))}
          </section>
        )}
      </>
    )}
  </main>
</PublicShell>
